
{"id":"0b7f0f39-da35-478c-baf1-a0a57063a06e","object":"chat.completion","created":1784991750,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    threshold = case['utility_threshold']\\n    node_map = {}\\n    children = {}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        nid = n['id']\\n        node_map[nid] = n\\n        children.setdefault(nid, [])\\n        parent = n.get('parent')\\n        if parent is not None:\\n            children.setdefault(parent, []).append(nid)\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda x: (-x['depth'], x['id']))\\n    queue = [n['id'] for n in sorted_nodes]\\n    from collections import deque\\n    q = deque(queue)\\n    removed = set()\\n    visit_order = []\\n    while q:\\n        nid = q.popleft()\\n        if nid in removed:\\n            continue\\n        visit_order.append(nid)\\n        node = node_map[nid]\\n        if any(cid not in removed for cid in children.get(nid, [])):\\n            continue\\n        if node['removable'] and node['utility'] <= threshold:\\n            removed.add(nid)\\n            parent = node.get('parent')\\n            if parent is not None and parent not in removed:\\n                q.append(parent)\\n    retained = [n['id'] for n in nodes if n['id'] not in removed]\\n    return {\\n        'retained_node_ids': retained,\\n        'visit_order': visit_order\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) that processes a tree of nodes with properties: id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility. The task: \"parse_tree_reduction_queue\". We need to maintain a queue, skip removed nodes, remove only a removable leaf whose utility is at most the threshold. After removal, enqueue its retained parent for reconsideration. Return retained_node_ids and visit_order.\n\nWe need to interpret the algorithm: Starting from the given nodes (list), we need to simulate a process of repeate